The potential vulnerability is related to a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability. This vulnerability occurs because the function generates a welcome message that will be rendered in an HTML page, and if the `username` parameter, which is user-supplied, is directly embedded into the HTML output without proper sanitization or encoding, an attacker could inject malicious client-side scripts. When another user views this message, the injected script would execute in their browser, potentially leading to session hijacking, defacement, or redirection to malicious sites.

